In 1942 everyone loved a soldier

2
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Yanks is a romance, drama, war film directed by John Schlesinger.

3
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:21,000
During WWII, the United States set up army bases in
Great Britain as part of the war effort.

4
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Against their proper sensibilities, many of the Brits don't much like the brash Yanks,
especially when it comes to the G.I.s making advances on the lonely British girls.

5
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:51,000
One relationship that develops is between married John, an Army Captain, and
the aristocratic Helen, whose naval husband is away at war.

6
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:36,000
Helen loves her husband, but Helen and John are looking for
some comfort during the difficult times.

7
00:40:15,000 --> 00:40:21,000
Matt Dyson, played by Richard Gere.

8
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Jean Moreton, played by Lisa Eichhorn.

9
00:51:45,000 --> 00:51:51,000
Helen, played by Vanessa Redgrave.

10
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:36,000
John, played by William Devane.

11
01:03:15,000 --> 01:03:21,000
Danny Ruffelo, played by Chick Vennera.

12
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
Mollie, played by Wendy Morgan.

13
01:14:45,000 --> 01:14:51,000
Yanks is a 1979 drama film directed by John Schlesinger, and produced by Joseph Janni
and Lester Persky, and is written by Colin Welland and Walter Bernstein.

14
01:20:30,000 --> 01:20:36,000
It stars Richard Gere, Lisa Eichhorn, Vanessa Redgrave, William Devane,
Chick Vennera, Wendy Morgan, Rachel Roberts and Tony Melody.

15
01:26:15,000 --> 01:26:21,000
The film is set during the Second World War in Northern
England and features no combat scenes.

16
01:32:00,000 --> 01:32:06,000
The film depicts the relationships between American soldiers stationed in semi-rural England
and the local population during the build-up to Operation Overlord in 1944.

17
01:37:45,000 --> 01:37:51,000
In particular, three romances between US service personnel and local women are shown, in order to explore the effects
of the cultural differences between the brash GIs or "Yanks" and the more reserved British population.

18
01:43:30,000 --> 01:43:36,000
The world premiere was held on 1 June 1979 at a cinema in Bournemouth, England.

19
01:49:15,000 --> 01:49:21,000
Lisa Eichhorn was present at the premiere, which had invited returning D-Day veterans
from many American divisions - most notably the American 29th Division.

20
01:55:00,000 --> 01:55:06,000
Leader of the returning 29ers was Sgt Curtis C.

21
02:00:45,000 --> 02:00:51,000
Williams who was 19 on D-Day.

22
02:06:30,000 --> 02:06:36,000
The film explores themes of new year's eve, northern
england, england, world war ii, prejudice.

23
02:12:15,000 --> 02:12:21,000
The tone is emotional.
